statement:** When the `--cluster-id` flag is used with the storage formatting tool, the formatter was stated to write **meta.properties V1**.\\n\\n**Final agreement:** The final agreement was to change this to write **meta.properties V2 format** instead.\\n\\n### Sources and Details\\n\\nThis discussion occurred in the KIP-1262 (Enable auto-formatting directories) mailing list thread:\\n\\n1. **Initial statement (from Jun Rao)** - in `/store/mail/mail-468c78200770789f37bb484d-0692112c.md` (March 27, 2026):\\n   > JR11. \\\"When --cluster-id is specified, the formatter writes meta.properties V1.\\\" It's a bit weird for the new code to write in V1 format. Could it write in V2 format?\\n\\n2. **Final agreement (Kevin Wu's response)** - in `/store/mail/2026-03-31-mail-c0e4cc4d441949adec4bdece-33866f43.md` (March 30-31, 2026):\\n   > RE JR11: Yeah, I think it is fine to write V2.\\n\\nJun Rao questioned why new code would write in the older V1 format, and Kevin Wu agreed that writing in V2 format would be appropriate instead.\",\"error\":null,\"files\":[\"store\",\"issues/KAFKA-20208/2026-02-23-created-update-meta-properties-ClusterIdRecord-d288f208.md\",\"mail/mail-468c78200770789f37bb484d-0692112c.md\",\"mail/2026-03-31-mail-c0e4cc4d441949adec4bdece-33866f43.md\"],\"seconds\":26.86,\"truncated\":false,\"turns\":3,\"usage\":{\"cache_read_tokens\":124385,\"cache_write_tokens\":23199,\"cost_usd\":0.06901750000000001,\"input_tokens\":66,\"output_tokens\":2023}}"}}}
